# Tier B: the thumbnail view over five thousand rows — the panel that is this app's own code.
#
# `many-fixture` rather than `bench-fixture`, because its .mp4/.txt mix is the point of the tile
# panel: a full-width row among tiles ends a line early. Settle does not wait for pictures, so
# `settle-thumbnails` is what makes "tiles on" mean "every visible tile has asked the shell and
# heard back". The retained-thumbnail cap (400) is what `mem` is there to show holding.

many-fixture 5000
go Many
flat on
assert-count 5000
time tiles.on thumbnails 0.5; settle-thumbnails
assert-realized under 200
time tiles.scroll list-scroll 100000; settle-thumbnails
assert-realized under 200
time tiles.back list-scroll 0; settle-thumbnails
time tiles.large thumbnails 1; settle-thumbnails
assert-realized under 200
assert-mem managed under 400
mem tiles
thumbnails 0
assert-not-launched
